//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Segregate Evens and Odds in a Linked List

Given a linked list, modify it such that all even numbers appear before all odd numbers. Preserve the relative order of nodes within each group.

NOTE: Don't create a new linked list, rearrange the provided one.

Examples:

Input:  17 -> 15 -> 8 -> 9 -> 2 -> 4 -> 6
Output: 8 -> 2 -> 4 -> 6 -> 17 -> 15 -> 9

Input:  1 -> 3 -> 5 -> 7
Output: 1 -> 3 -> 5 -> 7 (all odd, no change)

Input:  2 -> 4 -> 6 -> 8
Output: 2 -> 4 -> 6 -> 8 (all even, no change)

Constraints:
- 1 ≤ size of linked list ≤ 10^5
- 1 ≤ Each element ≤ 10^5

Time Complexity: O(n) - single pass
Space Complexity: O(1) - only 4 pointers used

